Data and separate writing materials
----------------------------------

The GPL-3 designation above applies to author-owned software. It does not
assert ownership of third-party datasets or replace their upstream terms.

ERP derives from the MNE sample audiovisual recording. Its public OpenNeuro
record ds000248, version 1.2.4, declares CC0 and credits Alexandre Gramfort
and Matti S. Hämäläinen. The dataset records preparation for BIDS by Alexandre Gramfort,
Mainak Jas, and Stefan Appelhoff. Source and declaration:
https://doi.org/10.18112/openneuro.ds000248.v1.2.4
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OpenNeuroDatasets/ds000248/0a357f1276dbf7fcc3c3fc35f74cb24ffe4a68a8/dataset_description.json
CC0 terms: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
MNE references: https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2013.00267 and
https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2013.10.027

The September 21, 2026 reconstruction of the pyRiemann 0.2.7 recipe matched
all 216 packaged ERP matrices to numerical precision, with exact label order.
The maximum relative Frobenius error was 5.56e-12; this is not a claim of
byte identity or reproduction of the original 2021 runtime. The matrices are
xDAWN prototype-augmented covariances of MEG test epochs from one participant.
The historical example credits Pedro Rodrigues and declares BSD 3-clause;
it is referenced rather than copied into this package:
https://github.com/pyRiemann/pyRiemann/blob/176e766f540bd4c7846f38573165fc3d27fc69ca/examples/ERP/plot_embedding_EEG.py

The gorilla configurations are redistributed under the upstream shapes 1.2.8
GPL-2 terms, retained separately from the author-owned GPL-3 software.
The GPL-2 text is supplied in LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt. The upstream archive
includes these coordinates and contains no observed data-specific exception.
Preserved attribution: Paul O'Higgins; O'Higgins and Dryden (1993),
Journal of Human Evolution 24, 183-205; Dryden and Mardia (2016), Chapter 1.
Riemann reorders landmarks by c(1, 5, 4, 3, 2, 8, 7, 6); coordinates and
individual ordering are otherwise identical to shapes::gorm.dat and
shapes::gorf.dat. This historical rearrangement was verified September 12,
2026; the present revision does not modify either dataset.
https://cran.r-project.org/package=shapes

Consult the dataset help and separate provenance reports for construction
